export const meta = {
  name: 'terminal-slowdown-investigation',
  description: 'Find why Superset terminals lag as more workspaces open, and why hook POSTs time out',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Investigate', detail: 'live census + two code traces in parallel' },
    { title: 'Synthesize', detail: 'rank causes against all evidence' },
    { title: 'Verify', detail: 'skeptic tries to refute each top cause' },
  ],
}

const REPO = 'C:\\Users\\khair\\Code Projects\\fork-superset-windows-arm64'

const CONTEXT = `
Context (Superset desktop fork, Windows 11 ARM64, repo ${REPO}, local main == origin/main):
- User has ~10-12 workspaces open, each running Claude Code in terminals. Typing and output in the terminals get very slow once several workspaces are open. The sidebar, sidebar selection and other apps stay fast.
- Known processes (re-resolve if they changed): Superset desktop PID 2588; host-service (node) PID 10432 on 127.0.0.1:48056; one python hook relay PID 41636 on 127.0.0.1:46817 (C:\\Users\\khair\\.superset\\hooks\\notify-daemon.json). All up since 2026-09-28 ~09:10.
- The relay forwards each Claude hook event to host-service /trpc/notifications.hook, 1.5 s per attempt, 4 s budget, answers 502 on failure. 166 timeouts 18:31-19:09 on 2026-10-01 in C:\\Users\\khair\\.superset\\agent-notify-hook.log and .log.1; also C:\\Users\\khair\\.superset\\logs\\dot-decisions.log. Relay source template: apps/desktop/src/main/lib/agent-jsonl-watcher/pane-map-hook.ts.
- C:\\Users\\khair\\AppData\\Roaming\\Superset\\logs\\main.log shows "presence" requests aborting about every 5 minutes.
- Claude Stop hooks: the http relay entry, plus a command hook C:\\Users\\khair\\.claude\\hooks\\cache-keepalive.ps1 (30 s timeout).
- AGENTS.md notes alternate-screen terminals are intentionally kept resident (eviction deferred).
Rules: strictly read-only. Do not edit files, do not kill or restart processes, do not POST to any local service. Scratch files only in ${REPO}\\tmp\\. Be terse.`

const FINDINGS = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    findings: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        properties: {
          claim: { type: 'string' },
          evidence: { type: 'string', description: 'file:line, log lines with timestamps, or measured numbers' },
          process: { type: 'string', description: 'which process/thread burns the time' },
          scales_with: { type: 'string', description: 'what makes it grow: workspaces, terminals, output volume, uptime, none' },
          confidence: { type: 'string', enum: ['proven', 'likely', 'possible'] },
        },
        required: ['claim', 'evidence', 'process', 'scales_with', 'confidence'],
      },
    },
    one_relay_or_many: { type: 'string', description: 'only for the live agent: answer, else empty' },
  },
  required: ['findings', 'one_relay_or_many'],
}

const INVESTIGATORS = [
  {
    key: 'live',
    agentType: 'sol',
    prompt: `${CONTEXT}

Your job: live measurement on this machine. Keep it under 10 minutes.
1. Process census: name, PID, parent PID, CPU seconds, working set for python/pythonw, node, claude, powershell/pwsh, bash, conhost, OpenConsole, Superset/electron. Group by parent. Is there exactly one hook relay or several? Any process per Claude session besides Claude itself (per hook event, per workspace)? Any leftover hook processes?
2. Read cache-keepalive.ps1. Does it start anything long-running or background per session? Are copies running now?
3. Sample 2 minutes every 3 s: CPU of host-service, desktop main, each renderer/GPU child, top 5 others. Report as % of ONE core so single-thread saturation shows (e.g. host-service pinned near 100% of one core while total CPU looks low).
4. Count live terminals/pty children under the host-service.
5. Bucket hook timeouts per hour across all relay logs: when did they start, steady or periodic, timeouts vs successes. Do they line up with main.log aborts?
6. Find the host-service's own logs if any; report slow-operation warnings or repeating jobs with timestamps.
Report findings with numbers and timestamps, and fill one_relay_or_many.`,
  },
  {
    key: 'terminal-path',
    agentType: 'astra',
    prompt: `${CONTEXT}

Your job: code trace of the terminal path. Find:
1. Path of a keystroke and of pty output: renderer xterm -> transport (websocket/IPC/tRPC subscription) -> host-service -> node-pty and back. Which process and thread runs each hop. file:line per hop.
2. Work done per output chunk per terminal in host-service or Electron main: headless xterm emulators/serializers for snapshot-restore, scrollback buffers, output scanning (links, agent status, OSC, titles, ports), disk logging, fan-out to subscribers. Do background/hidden workspaces' terminals still get fully parsed on the host-service thread? What does keeping alternate-screen terminals resident cost per chunk? Claude Code's TUI redraws constantly (spinner, status line), so per-chunk cost x number of sessions matters.
3. Renderer: do xterm instances of hidden workspaces stay mounted and render (WebGL contexts, render loops)? Would that lag terminals but not the sidebar?
Report each finding with file:line, the process/thread it burns, and what it scales with. fill one_relay_or_many with an empty string.`,
  },
  {
    key: 'host-service-load',
    agentType: 'astra',
    prompt: `${CONTEXT}

Your job: code trace of host-service load outside the pty byte stream. Find:
1. The notifications.hook handler: everything it awaits before replying (DB writes, git/child processes, file scans, network to the Pi usage service, phone/watch companion, relay, api.superset.sh, Electric). file:line.
2. The "presence" route the desktop calls: where it lives, what it awaits.
3. Every periodic job in host-service and Electron main: setInterval/setTimeout loops, resyncs (60 s status resync), janitors, retry loops (runtimeCleanupPendingAt), Claude account polling, agent-jsonl-watcher, git status polling, file watchers per worktree. For each: cadence, whether it does sync/blocking work on the event loop (execSync/spawnSync, *Sync fs over big trees, sync SQLite/libsql in loops, big JSON parse/stringify, full re-reads of growing files). Note anything near a 5-minute cadence.
4. Anything whose cost grows with uptime or with workspace/terminal/session count (unpruned maps, growing arrays, watchers never removed, logs re-read in full).
Report each finding with file:line, the process/thread it burns, and what it scales with. fill one_relay_or_many with an empty string.`,
  },
]

phase('Investigate')
const results = await parallel(INVESTIGATORS.map(inv => () =>
  agent(inv.prompt, { label: `investigate:${inv.key}`, phase: 'Investigate', agentType: inv.agentType, schema: FINDINGS })
    .then(r => r && { key: inv.key, ...r })))
const got = results.filter(Boolean)
const missing = INVESTIGATORS.map(i => i.key).filter(k => !got.some(g => g.key === k))
if (missing.length) log(`No result from: ${missing.join(', ')}`)
if (!got.length) throw new Error('All investigators failed')

phase('Synthesize')
const HYPOTHESES = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    hypotheses: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        properties: {
          title: { type: 'string' },
          mechanism: { type: 'string' },
          evidence: { type: 'string' },
          explains_terminal_only_lag: { type: 'boolean' },
          explains_hook_timeouts: { type: 'boolean' },
          explains_growth_with_workspaces: { type: 'boolean' },
          confidence: { type: 'string', enum: ['proven', 'likely', 'possible'] },
        },
        required: ['title', 'mechanism', 'evidence', 'explains_terminal_only_lag', 'explains_hook_timeouts', 'explains_growth_with_workspaces', 'confidence'],
      },
    },
    gaps: { type: 'string', description: 'what evidence is still missing' },
  },
  required: ['hypotheses', 'gaps'],
}
const synth = await agent(`${CONTEXT}

Three investigators reported. Combine their findings into at most 4 ranked hypotheses for: (a) terminal lag that grows with open workspaces while the sidebar stays fast, and (b) hook POSTs to host-service timing out past 1.5 s. Prefer one mechanism that explains both if the evidence supports it. Do not invent evidence; cite what the investigators found. You may read code or logs to check a claim (read-only).

Investigator reports:
${JSON.stringify(got, null, 1)}`, { label: 'synthesize', phase: 'Synthesize', schema: HYPOTHESES })
if (!synth) throw new Error('Synthesis failed')

phase('Verify')
const VERDICT = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    refuted: { type: 'boolean' },
    reason: { type: 'string' },
    extra_evidence: { type: 'string' },
  },
  required: ['refuted', 'reason', 'extra_evidence'],
}
const top = synth.hypotheses.slice(0, 3)
if (synth.hypotheses.length > 3) log(`Verifying top 3 of ${synth.hypotheses.length} hypotheses; the rest are returned unverified`)
const verified = await parallel(top.map((h, i) => () =>
  agent(`${CONTEXT}

Try to REFUTE this explanation for the terminal lag and hook timeouts. Check the code paths and, if useful, take light read-only measurements (no POSTs, no restarts). Look for: code that does not actually run in this setup, work that is async and cannot block, numbers that are too small to matter, or facts it fails to explain (sidebar stays fast; lag grows with open workspaces). Set refuted=true only with concrete evidence; if it survives, say what extra evidence supports it.

Hypothesis: ${JSON.stringify(h, null, 1)}`, { label: `verify:${i + 1}`, phase: 'Verify', agentType: 'astra', schema: VERDICT })
    .then(v => ({ ...h, verdict: v }))))

return { investigators: got, missing, hypotheses: verified, unverified: synth.hypotheses.slice(3), gaps: synth.gaps }

